WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.240
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:05.510 --> 00:09.347
It's the Seika era, in the democratic country of Nipponia.

3
00:09.848 --> 00:13.218
A huge ruling party has held power for a long time.

4
00:14.185 --> 00:18.056
This once-rich country is now on the edge of a cliff.

5
00:18.123 --> 00:20.325
The gap between rich and poor keeps growing.

6
00:20.391 --> 00:22.527
Both blue-collar workers and yakuza have no money.

7
00:23.428 --> 00:30.068
In Nagatanicho, the center of this nation, a great thief has landed.

8
00:30.135 --> 00:32.570
Her surname is Kisaragi, her given name is Yayoi.

9
00:32.637 --> 00:34.172
Weren't you an election consultant?

10
00:34.239 --> 00:37.041
I quit that and became Miyabi's secretary.

11
00:37.108 --> 00:39.077
I'm glad we had a fair fight.

12
00:39.144 --> 00:41.379
We should thank the great thief.

13
00:41.446 --> 00:43.615
A tanuki sniffing out the scent of money,

14
00:43.681 --> 00:45.750
and a tanuki sniffing out shadiness.

15
00:47.051 --> 00:49.754
The gong for this battle of deception is about to ring!

16
00:50.822 --> 00:52.423
PoliticaLupin!

17
00:55.860 --> 00:59.097
SECOND KAZAMATSURI CABINET SET TO START

18
01:26.157 --> 01:29.494
Hey, you lounging there. How did you get in?

19
01:29.561 --> 01:31.596
Doors of multi-purpose buildings take me only a minute.

20
01:31.663 --> 01:33.765
You should replace it with the latest lock.

21
01:33.831 --> 01:35.934
I shouldn't have lent a thief my room.

22
01:36.000 --> 01:39.671
I'm a great thief. Besides, the room you lent me can't really be called a room.

23
01:39.737 --> 01:43.374
It's a storage closet. No windows, bad airflow. It's the worst.

24
01:43.441 --> 01:44.542
If you hate it, get out.

25
01:44.609 --> 01:46.811
This place is close to Nagatanicho.

26
01:47.712 --> 01:50.281
Do you not enjoy seeing a cute girl every day?

27
01:50.848 --> 01:53.751
Hey, if you dare lay a hand on me, I'll kill you.

28
01:55.386 --> 01:56.721
Shut up, you squirt.

29
01:58.223 --> 01:59.123
Yes?

30
02:00.124 --> 02:01.192
Good morning, Mr. Kiuchi.

31
02:01.259 --> 02:03.228
Oh, good morning.

32
02:04.996 --> 02:06.164
Wait, just a second.

33
02:12.604 --> 02:14.072
I have a favor to ask.

34
02:14.906 --> 02:17.075
What is it? Should I tell Mr. Shiro?

35
02:17.141 --> 02:18.243
No, it's a secret.

36
02:23.748 --> 02:24.616
Mr. Kiuchi.

37
02:29.854 --> 02:30.922
Mr. Kiuchi.

38
02:31.489 --> 02:34.592
After using the "seasonal greetings" to pay for our expenses,

39
02:34.659 --> 02:37.662
this is the share split between me, Rui, and you, Inui.

40
02:37.729 --> 02:39.731
Isn't this a bit lacking? There was more, right?

41
02:39.797 --> 02:41.899
I made a political donation to Mr. Hachimaki.

42
02:41.966 --> 02:43.167
You mean that Hachimaki?

43
02:43.234 --> 02:46.070
He had to borrow money, and his deposit of three million was confiscated.

44
02:46.137 --> 02:48.006
So I asked Rui to donate to him.

45
02:48.072 --> 02:49.140
With stolen money?

46
02:49.207 --> 02:50.842
Money itself is blameless, you know.

47
02:50.908 --> 02:52.310
What a waste.

48
02:52.377 --> 02:56.314
I give half of the money I steal to people who don't have any.

49
02:56.381 --> 02:58.483
That's my policy, and I won't budge on it.

50
02:59.384 --> 03:01.786
No matter how clean a pond is,

51
03:01.853 --> 03:03.988
if you don't change the water and let it flow,

52
03:04.055 --> 03:07.425
it stagnates, turns muddy, and rots.

53
03:08.026 --> 03:10.962
The Cabinet rarely ever sees change, huh.

54
03:11.029 --> 03:14.532
Everything in Nagatanicho remains unchanged with near certainty.

55
03:14.599 --> 03:17.035
Because it never sees change, it's solid.

56
03:17.101 --> 03:21.005
That's why the real economic growth rate has stayed flat for 30 years.

57
03:21.072 --> 03:25.343
Aren't you going to change that, Mr. Natsume?

58
03:25.410 --> 03:28.246
Oh. We need to talk about the stolen election funds.

59
03:28.313 --> 03:30.415
This is Mr. Kiuchi's schedule of that day.

60
03:32.283 --> 03:36.554
Mr. Kiuchi said one of the secretaries was the culprit.

61
03:40.058 --> 03:42.560
He left the bag containing the cash right on the desk,

62
03:43.127 --> 03:46.097
and had left his seat a few times during that day.

63
03:50.134 --> 03:53.237
They are all paralyzed by suspicion and quite nervous now.

64
03:54.605 --> 03:57.642
Did Mr. Shiro tell you to investigate?

65
03:58.676 --> 04:00.712
If they find out I'm suspecting them,

66
04:00.778 --> 04:02.980
nobody is going to feel good about it.

67
04:03.614 --> 04:06.084
We can't just ask the Cabinet Intelligence to look into it.

68
04:06.150 --> 04:07.085
I'm honored, but…

69
04:07.151 --> 04:10.788
Natsume, I chose you because you know our secretaries so well.

70
04:12.590 --> 04:16.961
What a troublesome business. We aren't detectives!

71
04:17.028 --> 04:18.830
And that's not the only thing.

72
04:18.896 --> 04:20.031
Huh?

73
04:20.098 --> 04:23.368
The election funding issue has nothing to do with me.

74
04:23.434 --> 04:26.070
But isn't Chiba 17 the district you were in charge of?

75
04:26.137 --> 04:29.374
With all due respect, I was just helping out…

76
04:29.440 --> 04:33.878
The Financial Director is involved in all money matters.

77
04:35.279 --> 04:36.247
And besides…

78
04:36.314 --> 04:37.648
There's more?

79
04:37.715 --> 04:39.851
Secretary-General Kazamatsuri is also suspicious,

80
04:39.917 --> 04:43.421
and Mr. Shiro is defending his own secretary.

81
04:45.089 --> 04:46.791
Why don't you go probe around a bit?

82
04:48.092 --> 04:50.495
I made an effort to avoid getting close to anyone,

83
04:50.561 --> 04:53.131
and to maintain a proper distance,

84
04:53.197 --> 04:55.133
and the result of all of that

85
04:55.199 --> 04:57.635
is that all three of them

86
04:57.702 --> 05:01.973
think of me as their personal servant.

87
05:02.740 --> 05:06.878
Jeez…

88
05:06.944 --> 05:10.314
Don't give me more work.

89
05:10.381 --> 05:13.618
Who the hell stole that money?!

90
05:14.185 --> 05:17.955
How to get close to the safe in the Chief Cabinet Secretary's office…

91
05:18.656 --> 05:21.793
The current Chief Cabinet Secretary is Shokichi Takekoshi,

92
05:21.859 --> 05:23.294
the brother-in-law of Shiro Kobayakawa.

93
05:23.361 --> 05:25.797
Miyabi has hardly ever spoken to him.

94
05:26.798 --> 05:29.901
If we could get inside the Secretary's office we'd know what the layout is.

95
05:29.967 --> 05:33.070
If only Miyabi had been a member of the Kokuji party…

96
05:33.137 --> 05:36.441
If she held a position in the ruling party she could help us get close.

97
05:36.507 --> 05:39.243
I think so too.

98
05:39.811 --> 05:41.779
Join the Kokuji party.

99
05:41.846 --> 05:43.281
If you join the Kokuji party,

100
05:43.347 --> 05:45.950
you get ten million yen from party subsidies.

101
05:46.017 --> 05:48.586
Even if you lose the next election,

102
05:48.653 --> 05:50.922
you get one million yen a month.

103
05:50.988 --> 05:52.557
Already thinking about the next election?

104
05:52.623 --> 05:55.092
That's just the way politicians are.

105
05:56.127 --> 05:59.430
If we lose, the secretaries will be out of a job.

106
06:00.731 --> 06:02.767
We'll be dragging them down with us.

107
06:02.834 --> 06:04.469
I'm not joining the Kokuji party.

108
06:05.903 --> 06:07.271
I'm not joining.

109
06:07.772 --> 06:09.440
Talk her into it. You're good at that.

110
06:09.507 --> 06:11.042
I don't feel like it.

111
06:11.108 --> 06:14.011
I mean, that girl is dead serious.

112
06:16.347 --> 06:18.649
Miyabi is seriously

113
06:18.716 --> 06:20.952
and honestly trying to be a politician.

114
06:21.018 --> 06:22.353
You made her do that.

115
06:22.420 --> 06:25.056
It feels like I'm deceiving her.

116
06:25.122 --> 06:26.457
Because you are.

117
06:26.524 --> 06:29.560
If she had just a slightly more casual attitude about it,

118
06:29.627 --> 06:32.630
I could concentrate on my work with zero guilt.

119
06:32.697 --> 06:34.966
What a selfish thing to say.

120
06:35.032 --> 06:39.937
Anyway, I'll leave my main job aside for a moment and work for Miyabi's sake.

121
06:40.004 --> 06:42.073
I'll earn my paycheck. First is this.

122
06:42.139 --> 06:44.976
This account, Wasshi, which slandered Miyabi a lot.

123
06:45.042 --> 06:47.111
Oh, I saw this account a lot during the election.

124
06:50.081 --> 06:51.182
This post.

125
06:51.849 --> 06:55.052
"Miyabi Kobayakawa spent a lot of money on a host,

126
06:55.119 --> 06:57.455
got dumped, and got in a brawl outside. Have some shame!"

127
06:57.522 --> 06:59.657
Not even a tabloid would write stuff like this!

128
06:59.724 --> 07:01.859
The one who gave that host money was Miyabi's friend,

129
07:01.926 --> 07:03.361
and she was fighting for her!

130
07:03.427 --> 07:07.031
We have proof, so I had a lawyer file a disclosure request.

131
07:07.098 --> 07:10.801
Next, there is this. A video on NowTube.

132
07:11.469 --> 07:14.405
When I traced the source, it was a job-posting site.

133
07:14.906 --> 07:17.675
The site itself is ordinary,

134
07:17.742 --> 07:21.512
but multiple listings for creating "Miyabi Kobayakawa" videos popped up.

135
07:21.579 --> 07:26.083
Who made them create slanderous videos about Miyabi?

136
07:26.651 --> 07:27.752
And so,

137
07:28.352 --> 07:31.622
Rui applied for the video creation job and got hired!

138
07:31.689 --> 07:32.723
Huh?

139
07:32.790 --> 07:34.825
DIET MEMBERS' OFFICE

140
07:39.330 --> 07:41.666
Hello, Miss Miyabi.

141
07:41.732 --> 07:43.701
My name is Ginji.

142
07:44.402 --> 07:45.403
Masakado's…

143
07:46.137 --> 07:46.971
"Oi"?

144
07:47.738 --> 07:49.807
Oi? Is that an English word?

145
07:49.874 --> 07:53.678
It means I'm Masakado's older sister's son.

146
07:54.245 --> 07:55.680
How do you say that in English?

147
07:56.647 --> 07:57.648
"Nephew."

148
07:58.583 --> 07:59.417
Nephew?

149
07:59.483 --> 08:00.651
Nephew.

150
08:02.320 --> 08:04.055
Come on in.

151
08:04.555 --> 08:06.857
Which committee did you get assigned to?

152
08:06.924 --> 08:09.093
The Environment Committee.

153
08:10.061 --> 08:12.396
Many independents get put into that committee.

154
08:15.967 --> 08:16.801
Excuse me.

155
08:16.867 --> 08:19.904
Mr. Kiuchi, the secretary said that you, Mr. Honma,

156
08:19.971 --> 08:24.175
are a veteran with 40 years of experience as a secretary, and I should rely on you.

157
08:24.241 --> 08:25.576
For what?

158
08:25.643 --> 08:28.980
Neither I nor my secretaries know anything.

159
08:29.046 --> 08:32.717
I figured if I belonged to a party, there would be study sessions and such.

160
08:32.783 --> 08:35.519
A computer and telephone were provided for me,

161
08:35.586 --> 08:38.889
and since a vendor came by to pitch a multifunction printer, I ordered one.

162
08:39.624 --> 08:42.293
But what should I do from now on?

163
08:42.360 --> 08:43.527
Mr. Honma.

164
08:50.901 --> 08:52.603
Who are your secretaries?

165
08:52.670 --> 08:54.939
My chief public secretary

166
08:55.006 --> 08:56.273
is my friend Kaoru.

167
08:56.841 --> 08:59.110
She worked freelance as an interpreter.

168
08:59.677 --> 09:00.711
I see.

169
09:00.778 --> 09:03.648
My second public secretary is Momoko.

170
09:03.714 --> 09:06.217
She used to run a popular diner.

171
09:08.319 --> 09:10.321
I see!

172
09:11.022 --> 09:13.290
In other words, a group of amateurs.

173
09:13.357 --> 09:16.694
Kaoru majored in political science, and Momoko is quick with calculations.

174
09:19.363 --> 09:20.965
What about Yayoi Kisaragi?

175
09:21.032 --> 09:24.001
She's my private secretary. She didn't want to go public.

176
09:24.935 --> 09:25.903
She didn't want to?

177
09:25.970 --> 09:28.606
Public secretaries are paid with tax money, right?

178
09:29.240 --> 09:31.242
-Well, yes. -I prefer private.

179
09:31.308 --> 09:33.411
Make me your private secretary.

180
09:33.477 --> 09:36.247
I'm fine with being paid half as much. Consider me a part-time worker.

181
09:36.814 --> 09:39.250
I think her consulting work is keeping her busy.

182
09:39.316 --> 09:41.619
She said she was taking a break from consulting though.

183
09:41.686 --> 09:42.953
Is that so?

184
09:45.656 --> 09:47.224
If you want to make policies,

185
09:47.792 --> 09:50.027
have you found a policy secretary?

186
09:50.795 --> 09:52.797
A policy secretary?

187
09:53.798 --> 09:56.967
You can qualify by working as a lawyer or certified public accountant,

188
09:57.034 --> 09:59.770
or by being a secretary for ten years,

189
09:59.837 --> 10:02.440
after receiving the relevant certification.

190
10:02.506 --> 10:03.574
I've received it, too.

191
10:04.141 --> 10:05.676
Ten years as a secretary?

192
10:10.481 --> 10:12.950
If you join the Kokuji party, I can introduce you to someone.

193
10:14.218 --> 10:18.589
When you're in, you can learn everything about being a secretary and a politician.

194
10:18.656 --> 10:20.124
Right, Mr. Honma?

195
10:20.658 --> 10:21.525
Yes.

196
10:24.061 --> 10:26.630
Were you told by my father to invite me?

197
10:31.035 --> 10:34.472
Thank you for your time. Excuse me.

198
10:36.707 --> 10:37.975
-Nephew? -Nephew.

199
10:40.811 --> 10:44.281
Your recruiting skills are terrible.

200
10:44.348 --> 10:47.852
I talked to her. I did the bare minimum.

201
10:48.452 --> 10:50.554
Is the bare minimum all you need to do?

202
10:50.621 --> 10:54.358
You better give it your all. What the heck was that "nephew" stuff?

203
10:55.459 --> 10:57.595
I'm heading to the library.

204
10:59.130 --> 11:01.866
Such a nice place. Maybe I should move in too.

205
11:01.932 --> 11:02.767
There's a rooftop.

206
11:02.833 --> 11:04.168
-For a beer garden? -Or BBQ!

207
11:04.235 --> 11:05.436
The best parts of summer.

208
11:05.503 --> 11:06.337
Don't you dare.

209
11:06.403 --> 11:07.705
-You mean, do it? -Reverse psych?

210
11:07.772 --> 11:10.074
I meant it. You came to report, didn't you?

211
11:10.641 --> 11:12.710
How did that video-making gig turn out?

212
11:13.377 --> 11:14.645
Okay! Reporting!

213
11:15.379 --> 11:16.881
According to the job poster,

214
11:16.947 --> 11:19.850
they don't need videos of Miyabi Kobayakawa anymore.

215
11:19.917 --> 11:23.654
Instead, they sent me a script asking if I could make this kind of video.

216
11:23.721 --> 11:26.190
So I followed the script

217
11:26.257 --> 11:29.126
and made a video.

218
11:29.193 --> 11:30.060
This is it.

219
11:30.127 --> 11:33.130
Speechless! Foreigners are splurging welfare money!

220
11:33.197 --> 11:35.733
An extinction threat! Nipponia is turning into a trash heap!

221
11:35.800 --> 11:38.002
The taxes you paid…

222
11:38.068 --> 11:40.738
I ignored my own feelings and worked on it.

223
11:40.805 --> 11:44.008
It was done really quickly, and the client liked it.

224
11:44.074 --> 11:45.776
And after some flattering,

225
11:45.843 --> 11:47.978
we talked directly on Descord.

226
11:48.546 --> 11:52.483
Why did you make videos criticizing Miyabi?

227
11:52.550 --> 11:54.952
Political videos do well during elections.

228
11:55.019 --> 11:59.023
Miyabi videos were trending. I might earn 400,000 yen next month.

229
11:59.089 --> 12:01.292
Amazing. Respect!

230
12:01.358 --> 12:02.193
Thanks.

231
12:02.259 --> 12:03.894
Dad, play with me!

232
12:03.961 --> 12:06.831
Quiet, Dad is working now.

233
12:09.133 --> 12:13.437
Anyway, the Miyabi videos are so last season. We do this now.

234
12:13.504 --> 12:15.039
"Foreigners are dangerous" videos.

235
12:15.105 --> 12:19.777
Is the info in the script I got really true?

236
12:19.844 --> 12:21.612
It seems in reality,

237
12:21.679 --> 12:25.082
foreign households only take up 3% of welfare funds, not 33% like the script.

238
12:26.217 --> 12:27.985
I don't know and don't care.

239
12:28.552 --> 12:32.189
A complete lack of morals. Well, a thief like me can't say much.

240
12:32.256 --> 12:36.493
Wait, their goal is just making money?

241
12:36.560 --> 12:38.829
-It seems so. -It will be hard to stop those!

242
12:38.896 --> 12:41.265
Sometimes foreign forces do it too.

243
12:41.332 --> 12:43.767
Moneymaking and political agendas.

244
12:43.834 --> 12:48.105
With "phone farms," you can fake viewer counts.

245
12:48.172 --> 12:51.108
If you get a good amount of views in, the video goes trending,

246
12:51.175 --> 12:52.576
which gets it even more views.

247
12:52.643 --> 12:53.477
It never ends.

248
12:54.211 --> 12:56.146
It's rage bait.

249
12:56.213 --> 12:59.383
Designed to make people react in anger. Modern alchemy.

250
12:59.450 --> 13:01.652
How did the disclosure request against Wasshi go?

251
13:01.719 --> 13:04.788
Wasshi's videos were from a company called Ponz Next.

252
13:04.855 --> 13:06.557
Their capital is ten million yen.

253
13:06.624 --> 13:09.560
They are a web and ad company, it seems,

254
13:09.627 --> 13:11.562
but there is no more info online.

255
13:11.629 --> 13:13.964
Meaning someone is posting while slacking off at work?

256
13:14.031 --> 13:14.965
Maybe?

257
13:15.032 --> 13:17.101
Employee or part-timer, who knows.

258
13:17.167 --> 13:18.435
Ponz Next…

259
13:19.336 --> 13:21.705
I remember it from a political funding report.

260
13:21.772 --> 13:23.207
POLITICAL FUNDING RECEIPT DATABASE

261
13:23.274 --> 13:24.742
PONZ NEXT

262
13:26.343 --> 13:27.945
More results than I thought.

263
13:28.012 --> 13:30.547
The scent of money! Let's investigate.

264
13:30.614 --> 13:32.283
You guys can't handle this.

265
13:34.685 --> 13:36.186
This is my specialty.

266
13:44.962 --> 13:46.430
-Momo. -Yes?

267
13:46.497 --> 13:50.668
Just how busy is Yayoi with her consulting work?

268
13:50.734 --> 13:53.871
Huh? I think she isn't busy at all.

269
13:53.938 --> 13:56.674
She used to be a regular at my shop.

270
13:56.740 --> 13:59.610
She doesn't have that much money either.

271
14:01.011 --> 14:03.447
I'll go search for cheap Chiba properties.

272
14:03.514 --> 14:05.816
Somewhere convenient, easy for people to visit.

273
14:05.883 --> 14:08.152
Cheapness comes first, then convenience.

274
14:08.218 --> 14:09.553
I'm off.

275
14:09.620 --> 14:11.121
-Take care. -Take care.

276
14:12.456 --> 14:14.591
Hey, we received this.

277
14:14.658 --> 14:18.429
"The Women Lawmakers' League for Promoting Women in Politics."

278
14:18.495 --> 14:21.865
Hosted by Misaki Utsunomiya of the Minyu Party.

279
14:21.932 --> 14:26.103
Multi-party. Even independents can join. Shall we check it out?

280
14:26.837 --> 14:31.542
The women's restroom on the second floor of the Lower House

281
14:31.608 --> 14:35.145
has only a quarter as many stalls as the men's.

282
14:35.212 --> 14:38.449
As you may know, it always has long lines.

283
14:39.116 --> 14:42.086
We'll have more and more female Diet members.

284
14:42.152 --> 14:45.856
If we don't start renovation now, it will be too late.

285
14:46.523 --> 14:49.026
We will strongly demand this.

286
14:49.093 --> 14:53.297
If we don't speak up, nothing changes.

287
14:53.897 --> 14:54.898
Thank you for today.

288
14:56.133 --> 14:57.434
Welcome.

289
14:58.002 --> 14:59.269
I'm the host, Utsunomiya.

290
15:00.237 --> 15:01.872
-I'm Miyabi… -Kobayakawa.

291
15:01.939 --> 15:05.242
I watched your election. It was exhilarating.

292
15:05.309 --> 15:06.343
Thanks.

293
15:07.711 --> 15:11.348
Are you okay? You must feel really lost right now.

294
15:11.415 --> 15:13.117
I'm completely lost.

295
15:13.183 --> 15:14.051
Yeah.

296
15:14.118 --> 15:15.152
-Ms. Matsushita. -Yes.

297
15:15.719 --> 15:18.188
She is my secretary. Ask her anything you don't know.

298
15:19.390 --> 15:21.291
-Thank you. -Pleased to meet you.

299
15:21.358 --> 15:25.763
I'm sure you already know, but politics is an old-men's paradise.

300
15:25.829 --> 15:26.563
Yes.

301
15:27.965 --> 15:31.001
If women connect and make work easier,

302
15:31.068 --> 15:32.536
more women will be elected.

303
15:32.603 --> 15:36.907
Then we can push policies in untouched areas.

304
15:36.974 --> 15:39.576
This is the kind of forward-thinking our league upholds.

305
15:39.643 --> 15:41.578
Please let me join.

306
15:41.645 --> 15:43.414
You're very welcome.

307
15:44.048 --> 15:46.850
I belong to about ten other leagues.

308
15:46.917 --> 15:49.319
There are many cross-party members, so if you're interested…

309
15:49.887 --> 15:50.754
I am!

310
15:53.424 --> 15:56.293
Don't rush. Look closely, then decide.

311
15:56.360 --> 15:58.462
Each has costs and dues.

312
15:59.930 --> 16:02.132
Sometimes you pay out of pocket.

313
16:02.199 --> 16:03.133
I see.

314
16:04.068 --> 16:07.004
KOKUJI PARTY

315
16:07.704 --> 16:09.573
What is your business?

316
16:09.640 --> 16:11.308
SADAHARU IENAGA

317
16:11.375 --> 16:14.011
It isn't really urgent, but…

318
16:17.114 --> 16:18.816
I heard you objected

319
16:18.882 --> 16:22.719
to the election budget allocation

320
16:22.786 --> 16:25.956
that the Secretary General and I made.

321
16:26.523 --> 16:29.560
What is your reason?

322
16:29.626 --> 16:30.727
I…

323
16:30.794 --> 16:34.631
In the House election, the Kokuji Party didn't gain seats.

324
16:35.132 --> 16:38.735
We lost seats. Do you feel responsible?

325
16:39.837 --> 16:42.005
I was appointed Finance Director…

326
16:43.340 --> 16:44.541
So…

327
16:47.377 --> 16:48.812
My main duty

328
16:49.313 --> 16:52.616
is simply handling party accounts.

329
16:52.683 --> 16:54.852
Handling party accounts?

330
16:57.187 --> 16:59.823
Your job is to stamp.

331
17:00.390 --> 17:02.259
Just stamp the documents.

332
17:02.326 --> 17:06.430
Stamp the documents we tell you to stamp.

333
17:06.997 --> 17:10.100
That's your job as Finance Director.

334
17:10.934 --> 17:11.768
Understand?

335
17:13.570 --> 17:15.139
Do you understand?

336
17:15.205 --> 17:16.140
Yes.

337
17:23.347 --> 17:24.848
May I join you?

338
17:27.684 --> 17:28.552
Go ahead.

339
17:34.224 --> 17:35.526
No appetite?

340
17:36.293 --> 17:37.294
Not really.

341
17:40.464 --> 17:43.333
Eel is going extinct, yet it's on the menu, huh.

342
17:43.400 --> 17:44.601
Let's eat.

343
17:49.873 --> 17:51.875
You eat it knowing that?

344
17:52.442 --> 17:54.545
Don't you feel doubt?

345
17:54.611 --> 17:58.849
If it's sold, I eat it. Like if there's money, I take it.

346
17:58.916 --> 18:03.020
If you can make money writing lies online, you would do it, right?

347
18:03.086 --> 18:03.954
Would you do it?

348
18:04.021 --> 18:04.855
You wouldn't?

349
18:04.922 --> 18:05.889
I wouldn't.

350
18:05.956 --> 18:09.826
Even if most wouldn't, some will. Humans are evil creatures.

351
18:09.893 --> 18:11.795
You believe in original sin?

352
18:11.862 --> 18:14.198
I prefer believing people are good.

353
18:14.264 --> 18:16.934
Me too. But the world isn't like that.

354
18:17.000 --> 18:19.570
You must design systems so it's hard to do evil,

355
18:19.636 --> 18:21.238
or it fills with evil people.

356
18:21.305 --> 18:22.739
For now, eel is being sold,

357
18:22.806 --> 18:25.409
so the world is full of eel-eating evil people.

358
18:26.410 --> 18:28.845
When I eat eel,

359
18:29.713 --> 18:32.449
I eat with the intent to drive eels extinct.

360
18:35.085 --> 18:37.688
Research on farmed eel is progressing.

361
18:37.754 --> 18:42.359
The Fisheries Agency put 700 million yen in last year's supplementary budget

362
18:42.426 --> 18:45.262
into artificial eel research and rollout.

363
18:45.329 --> 18:47.064
Artificial eels will be on tables soon.

364
18:47.130 --> 18:49.099
Wonderful story. Bad people will disappear.

365
18:49.166 --> 18:52.936
Saving eel from extinction is also a politician's job.

366
18:54.938 --> 18:57.841
Can politics solve Internet fake news?

367
19:01.511 --> 19:03.413
It's dangerous for those in power

368
19:04.214 --> 19:06.917
to get to decide what is "fake news".

369
19:06.984 --> 19:08.919
Nipponia has freedom of expression.

370
19:08.986 --> 19:10.454
Really.

371
19:11.388 --> 19:13.023
Personally,

372
19:13.857 --> 19:18.495
I think we could demonetize videos related to politics,

373
19:18.562 --> 19:20.264
at least during elections.

374
19:20.330 --> 19:21.798
That's very helpful.

375
19:22.799 --> 19:28.572
I'm thinking of asking a company to handle slander against Miyabi.

376
19:28.639 --> 19:29.740
Maybe you need it.

377
19:30.307 --> 19:32.576
Would this company be good? Do you know it?

378
19:39.082 --> 19:41.351
PONZ NEXT

379
19:50.127 --> 19:54.498
Many Diet members seem to use this company.

380
19:55.732 --> 19:58.769
I don't recommend it.

381
19:58.835 --> 20:00.237
Huh? Why?

382
20:00.304 --> 20:03.040
I think they only accept jobs from Kokuji Party members.

383
20:06.343 --> 20:10.681
Do you know this account that slandered Miyabi?

384
20:12.449 --> 20:14.217
WASSHI

385
20:14.284 --> 20:16.553
Looking back,

386
20:16.620 --> 20:18.622
it's not just Miyabi.

387
20:18.689 --> 20:21.358
Many opposition members are slandered too.

388
20:21.425 --> 20:23.427
In many cases, it borders on defamation.

389
20:23.493 --> 20:26.196
If that's all, then this would just be a common malicious account.

390
20:26.263 --> 20:28.131
But I noticed something big.

391
20:28.632 --> 20:31.335
It's active on weekdays from nine to six,

392
20:31.401 --> 20:32.869
and off on weekends and holidays.

393
20:32.936 --> 20:34.204
Like a salaryman.

394
20:34.271 --> 20:36.340
Ponz Next is doing it as a job.

395
20:37.674 --> 20:39.943
The one ordering it is the Kokuji Party.

396
20:41.978 --> 20:44.581
The president of Ponz Next is Uchiteru Tomino.

397
20:44.648 --> 20:47.150
This guy himself isn't a big deal.

398
20:47.918 --> 20:50.654
His relative is a big shot.

399
20:52.422 --> 20:55.926
The executive secretary of the Kokuji Party, Sadaharu Ienaga.

400
20:55.992 --> 20:57.194
-A politician? -No.

401
20:57.260 --> 20:59.930
Not Ienaga. This guy is a Kokuji Party staff member.

402
21:00.497 --> 21:03.767
He climbed the ranks and has been the treasurer for over 50 years.

403
21:03.834 --> 21:06.703
Thanks to that, even cabinet ministers can't talk back to him.

404
21:06.770 --> 21:08.238
Isn't Natsume the treasurer?

405
21:08.305 --> 21:11.274
The Finance Director is just a title. The real power rests with Ienaga.

406
21:11.341 --> 21:13.143
What the heck? What?

407
21:13.210 --> 21:15.178
This, this, and this too.

408
21:16.747 --> 21:19.015
These are companies with ties to Ienaga,

409
21:19.082 --> 21:21.351
taking on work from the Kokuji Party.

410
21:22.185 --> 21:25.155
There's a rumor that this research company

411
21:25.222 --> 21:27.891
took a job for 50 million yen and got a 20 million yen kickback.

412
21:27.958 --> 21:31.695
What a dark treasure. Is Ponz Next doing that too?

413
21:31.762 --> 21:32.963
Probably.

414
21:33.530 --> 21:36.066
My request for disclosure got accepted.

415
21:38.402 --> 21:42.105
Ponz Next was behind this Wasshi account.

416
21:42.606 --> 21:44.708
They pretended to be civilians

417
21:46.777 --> 21:49.413
to spread bad rumors about your opposition and rivals.

418
21:50.180 --> 21:52.949
Where is the money coming from? It's tax money, right?

419
21:53.016 --> 21:54.384
With all respect,

420
21:54.451 --> 21:57.721
even if some members have deals with them,

421
21:57.788 --> 22:00.490
we can't say the slander is the Kokuji Party's request.

422
22:02.292 --> 22:06.430
I don't want a lawsuit. It's troublesome, you know.

423
22:07.164 --> 22:11.435
If you could at least delete the rumors about Miyabi,

424
22:12.002 --> 22:15.705
I could stay a see-no-evil, hear-no-evil monkey.

425
22:20.110 --> 22:23.513
I'm actually pretty angry.

426
22:26.683 --> 22:28.685
Hello. Everyone working hard?

427
22:28.752 --> 22:30.253
-Yes! -I got food.

428
22:30.320 --> 22:32.088
Yay!

429
22:32.155 --> 22:33.523
I'll call Miyabi.

430
22:36.426 --> 22:38.261
Did you find a Chiba office?

431
22:38.328 --> 22:39.796
It's hard.

432
22:39.863 --> 22:42.566
Even though she's a Kobayakawa daughter,

433
22:42.632 --> 22:45.101
they won't rent to someone who beat a Kokuji Party member.

434
22:45.168 --> 22:47.504
All the landlords are Kokuji Party people.

435
22:47.571 --> 22:49.806
All of them… It's a wonder we won.

436
22:49.873 --> 22:52.309
By 210 votes. A miracle!

437
22:52.375 --> 22:53.910
Yayoi.

438
22:53.977 --> 22:55.345
How did your consulting go?

439
22:55.412 --> 22:56.346
It went fine today.

440
22:58.248 --> 23:00.283
What is everyone doing now?

441
23:02.552 --> 23:05.722
We're making a league for election reform.

442
23:05.789 --> 23:08.124
-Wow! -Yes!

443
23:08.191 --> 23:09.826
-A league? -Of Diet members.

444
23:09.893 --> 23:10.961
Here.

445
23:13.029 --> 23:16.500
To submit a bill in the Lower House, we need 20 members.

446
23:16.566 --> 23:19.536
So it all starts with gathering supporters.

447
23:19.603 --> 23:22.839
Now we're preparing materials for the first meeting.

448
23:23.907 --> 23:24.875
I'll help.

449
23:32.649 --> 23:35.785
Do you know Ponz Next?

450
23:36.353 --> 23:38.421
Yes, it's related to Mr. Ienaga, right?

451
23:38.488 --> 23:39.356
Exactly.

452
23:39.422 --> 23:41.925
That company not only does PR,

453
23:41.992 --> 23:45.095
but also operates accounts that spread slander.

454
23:45.161 --> 23:46.229
No way.

455
23:46.296 --> 23:48.798
Hard to believe, but I looked into it…

456
23:52.602 --> 23:54.571
It received more than 25 million yen

457
23:54.638 --> 23:56.439
from the Kokuji Party Tokyo chapter,

458
23:56.506 --> 23:58.441
aside from donations by other Diet members.

459
23:58.508 --> 24:01.111
We can't say they aren't affiliated with us.

460
24:01.177 --> 24:05.382
This is terrible! I can't believe they chose this sloppy method.

461
24:09.519 --> 24:13.557
What happens if I make this public?

462
24:14.791 --> 24:15.892
You would be cut off.

463
24:16.660 --> 24:19.062
Right?!

464
24:25.001 --> 24:27.671
I want to get angry, but I can't…

465
24:28.405 --> 24:32.576
Maybe we should cut off Natsume?

466
24:33.643 --> 24:34.778
Your son

467
24:35.445 --> 24:38.815
refused his own party's support speech, didn't he?

468
24:38.882 --> 24:43.086
Maybe Mr. Natsume has been a bad influence.

469
24:43.653 --> 24:45.188
Otherwise,

470
24:45.255 --> 24:48.124
there's no reason we would have lost Chiba 17.

471
24:50.794 --> 24:52.963
We even used real money.

472
24:53.797 --> 24:56.633
There was some trouble there…

473
24:56.700 --> 24:59.135
Our boy is hard to handle.

474
24:59.202 --> 25:02.105
I raised him too gently.

475
25:03.273 --> 25:05.508
Natsume is capable.

476
25:05.575 --> 25:07.010
Colorless.

477
25:07.811 --> 25:09.713
Not tied to any faction. I like that about him.

478
25:10.880 --> 25:14.884
Please go easy on him.

479
25:16.553 --> 25:19.322
If you say so…

480
25:19.389 --> 25:20.357
Yes.

481
25:28.531 --> 25:30.900
-Here. -I'll go to the House of Councillors.

482
25:30.967 --> 25:32.369
-Okay. -Here.

483
25:32.435 --> 25:34.070
Then I'll go to the House of Representatives.

484
25:34.137 --> 25:35.071
I'm going too.

485
25:50.053 --> 25:51.588
ELECTION REFORM LEAGUE

486
25:51.655 --> 25:54.057
After we've gathered people for the league, what next?

487
25:56.393 --> 26:00.363
Consult the House research office, hear from experts,

488
26:00.430 --> 26:03.867
deepen discussion, and firm up the bill.

489
26:03.933 --> 26:07.103
Also have National Diet Library staff

490
26:07.170 --> 26:11.341
look into foreign precedents and past data.

491
26:11.408 --> 26:13.309
Okay. Mic is ready.

492
26:14.244 --> 26:16.246
Did you find a policy secretary?

493
26:16.312 --> 26:18.114
We're recruiting on social media.

494
26:18.181 --> 26:20.150
I hope you find someone good.

495
26:20.216 --> 26:22.419
Oh, it's almost time.

496
26:31.728 --> 26:33.229
I'll take a look.

497
26:47.610 --> 26:50.313
Sorry for being late.

498
26:50.380 --> 26:52.615
Oh, it's okay.

499
27:00.457 --> 27:03.326
Will it be hard as an independent?

500
27:03.393 --> 27:04.728
Well…

501
27:04.794 --> 27:08.231
It's easier with horizontal connections.

502
27:09.199 --> 27:13.069
In your case, gathering 20 people might take five years.

503
27:13.136 --> 27:14.070
Five years?

504
27:14.137 --> 27:16.573
A league about rethinking hereditary politics

505
27:16.639 --> 27:19.976
won't do well with Kokuji members, many of whom come from political families.

506
27:20.043 --> 27:23.313
Opposition members see you as Shiro Kobayakawa's daughter

507
27:23.379 --> 27:24.581
and keep away.

508
27:24.647 --> 27:29.085
You must show each person who you are to gain their understanding,

509
27:29.152 --> 27:32.589
earn their trust, and gather 20 people.

510
27:32.655 --> 27:36.626
Then five more years of discussion.

511
27:36.693 --> 27:38.728
Ten years total.

512
27:38.795 --> 27:40.530
That's pretty standard.

513
27:40.597 --> 27:43.099
One of my leagues

514
27:43.166 --> 27:45.969
is only now ready for deliberation,

515
27:46.970 --> 27:48.605
after eight years.

516
27:50.140 --> 27:52.942
For a first-term independent, it will take longer.

517
27:54.611 --> 27:57.480
Can I join the Minyu Party?

518
27:57.547 --> 28:00.583
It's a possible path, right? They're the top opposition party.

519
28:00.650 --> 28:03.653
I thought so too, and asked our party leader.

520
28:04.320 --> 28:07.290
No. Not even a chance.

521
28:07.357 --> 28:11.461
They fear you might leak info to your father. They don't trust you.

522
28:12.428 --> 28:14.964
Probably every party is the same.

523
28:17.767 --> 28:20.937
DIET MEMBERS' OFFICE

524
28:25.608 --> 28:26.442
Come in.

525
28:26.509 --> 28:28.178
I'm back!

526
28:28.244 --> 28:29.813
-Thank you. -We're back.

527
28:31.614 --> 28:33.082
Thanks.

528
28:33.149 --> 28:34.184
Oh, you can drink it?

529
28:34.250 --> 28:36.286
They sell it at the convenience store downstairs.

530
28:36.352 --> 28:38.955
Look, "Prime Minister Kazamatsuri Dumplings."

531
28:39.022 --> 28:42.158
Almost expired! Really? It was at half price.

532
28:43.259 --> 28:45.361
Hey, I got your favorite too, Miyabi.

533
28:46.763 --> 28:48.631
Maybe I bought too much.

534
28:52.902 --> 28:55.505
Maybe I should join the Kokuji Party.

535
28:56.072 --> 28:57.974
That will solve everything.

536
28:58.041 --> 29:00.743
We could rent the Chiba office

537
29:01.511 --> 29:03.479
and not make everyone jobless.

538
29:03.546 --> 29:05.081
Jobless…

539
29:05.148 --> 29:07.050
Don't worry about four years from now.

540
29:07.116 --> 29:11.187
What if the House is dissolved in two years? Two years go by fast.

541
29:11.254 --> 29:13.723
We are just, you know…

542
29:13.790 --> 29:16.993
Temp workers who wandered in here.

543
29:18.328 --> 29:20.763
Momo, you can do anything, and it's super helpful.

544
29:20.830 --> 29:22.365
Thanks!

545
29:22.432 --> 29:25.735
Kaoru too, you quit interpreting to come here.

546
29:25.802 --> 29:29.205
I'm having fun being involved in politics.

547
29:29.272 --> 29:30.306
I'm excited.

548
29:30.373 --> 29:34.043
But we never got involved. They don't even take us seriously.

549
29:34.777 --> 29:35.945
I got elected,

550
29:36.679 --> 29:39.415
got carried away, and misunderstood.

551
29:39.916 --> 29:43.686
No one visits us. I'm so unpopular it's funny.

552
29:44.854 --> 29:45.788
When I think about it,

553
29:45.855 --> 29:49.125
the reason I don't want to join the Kokuji Party

554
29:50.860 --> 29:53.329
is that it feels like losing to my father.

555
29:54.364 --> 29:56.866
That's all. A child's selfishness.

556
29:57.700 --> 30:01.571
Some people voted for me because I'm not in the ruling party.

557
30:01.638 --> 30:05.174
I would have to explain to them,

558
30:06.309 --> 30:08.077
but it's the only way.

559
30:09.779 --> 30:12.982
Are you fine with this, Miyabi?

560
30:17.387 --> 30:19.889
I don't want this to end without being able to do anything.

561
30:21.891 --> 30:25.528
Maybe I can use the Kokuji Party.

562
30:27.130 --> 30:30.733
Regardless of my old man, I am me.

563
30:31.567 --> 30:32.969
I'm a Diet member.

564
30:34.237 --> 30:36.639
That's right. We can still do what we want.

565
30:37.674 --> 30:41.477
Let's use the Kokuji Party to the fullest.

566
30:41.544 --> 30:42.545
Yeah.

567
30:46.115 --> 30:47.850
-Let's toast! -Yeah.

568
30:48.985 --> 30:50.253
You have one too.

569
30:50.320 --> 30:52.121
-Me too. -Okay.

570
30:57.493 --> 30:58.494
What?

571
31:02.799 --> 31:04.367
What are you drinking there?

572
31:05.969 --> 31:07.270
Barley tea.

573
31:13.042 --> 31:15.878
Isn't that the most expensive one? I even put it away!

574
31:15.945 --> 31:17.814
I'm drinking to drown my sorrows.

575
31:17.880 --> 31:21.284
Joining the Kokuji Party is great, isn't it?

576
31:21.351 --> 31:22.952
I don't like it.

577
31:23.019 --> 31:24.721
Don't be picky.

578
31:24.787 --> 31:27.156
Something doesn't sit well with me.

579
31:27.924 --> 31:29.258
What?

580
31:29.325 --> 31:31.995
Now Wasshi won't slander her anymore.

581
31:32.061 --> 31:33.329
It's all good.

582
31:36.866 --> 31:38.601
-Huh? -"Huh" what?

583
31:38.668 --> 31:42.238
"If we join those slanderers, we won't be slandered anymore!"

584
31:42.305 --> 31:44.040
"Hooray!" Can you be happy about that?

585
31:44.107 --> 31:47.276
Wasshi is still happily slandering people.

586
31:47.343 --> 31:49.178
Miyabi's rumors haven't been deleted

587
31:49.245 --> 31:52.215
and will keep being used by people looking to make money.

588
31:52.281 --> 31:53.983
That's the law of the Internet.

589
31:54.050 --> 31:56.085
That law can eat shit!

590
31:56.152 --> 31:58.554
I'll decide what I get angry about.

591
31:59.122 --> 32:03.860
So I made a new account.

592
32:03.926 --> 32:05.395
Meet "Usshi"!

593
32:05.461 --> 32:06.462
USSHI AN ACCOUNT THAT POSTS THE TRUTH

594
32:06.529 --> 32:08.131
PONZ NEXT

595
32:09.599 --> 32:12.068
Boss? Boss!

596
32:13.102 --> 32:14.537
This video!

597
32:15.104 --> 32:16.005
Video?

598
32:16.072 --> 32:17.273
WASSHI = PONZ NEXT

599
32:18.141 --> 32:20.810
The truth! Ponz Next is the company behind the Wasshi account.

600
32:20.877 --> 32:23.413
This social media account slanders politicians

601
32:23.479 --> 32:26.282
on orders of the Kokuji Party.

602
32:26.349 --> 32:29.819
The account known as "Wasshi" is run by Ponz Next Inc.

603
32:29.886 --> 32:32.889
It is a website and ad company,

604
32:32.955 --> 32:36.993
but it posts on weekdays from nine to six, fully off on weekends and holidays.

605
32:37.060 --> 32:38.428
Like a salaryman.

606
32:38.494 --> 32:40.063
The president of Ponz Next

607
32:40.129 --> 32:42.131
is a relative of the bureau chief

608
32:42.198 --> 32:44.867
who has been the Kokuji Party's treasurer for many years.

609
32:44.934 --> 32:48.704
Here is evidence showing the connection between Ponz Next and the Kokuji Party.

610
32:48.771 --> 32:53.242
I will repost this video on NowTube

611
32:53.309 --> 32:55.411
and ask a phone farm

612
32:55.478 --> 32:57.213
to get it to trending!

613
32:58.281 --> 33:00.149
Then, lo and behold.

614
33:01.017 --> 33:04.687
It will look like this kind of video is trending,

615
33:04.754 --> 33:08.758
so now tons of other videos like it appear!

616
33:08.825 --> 33:10.827
Ponz Next is trending.

617
33:12.695 --> 33:14.163
HIRING VIDEO EDITORS

618
33:14.230 --> 33:17.567
POPULAR TOPIC "WASSHI" EXLANATION VIDEO CREATION

619
33:17.633 --> 33:20.670
The origin of the posts by the slandering account Wasshi

620
33:20.736 --> 33:22.738
is a company called Ponz Next…

621
33:23.973 --> 33:26.709
There are also rumors that the Kokuji Party has deep ties with it…

622
33:26.776 --> 33:28.444
This is seriously funny.

623
33:28.511 --> 33:31.414
IS THE KOKUJI PARTY INVOLVED IN THIS?!

624
33:36.352 --> 33:38.154
UPPER HOUSE LOWER HOUSE

625
33:42.592 --> 33:45.027
Kisaragi, that video…

626
33:45.695 --> 33:46.762
Did you make it?

627
33:52.368 --> 33:54.770
Huh, I thought you did it…

628
33:54.837 --> 33:55.671
What?

629
33:55.738 --> 33:58.808
It's exactly what we talked about.

630
33:58.875 --> 34:01.644
I thought Natsume wanted to whistleblow for justice.

631
34:01.711 --> 34:02.979
No, I…

632
34:05.515 --> 34:08.584
Someone heard what we said.

633
34:09.785 --> 34:12.788
Nagatanicho is not to be trusted.

634
34:12.855 --> 34:13.923
Excuse me.

635
34:19.162 --> 34:20.196
THEIR BOSS IS A RELATIVE OF A PARTY OFFICIAL

636
34:20.263 --> 34:21.631
Two weeks ago,

637
34:21.697 --> 34:24.167
a disclosure request on Wasshi's posts came in,

638
34:24.233 --> 34:28.304
and our IP address was disclosed to Miyabi Kobayakawa's office.

639
34:28.371 --> 34:30.406
That's about the extent of it.

640
34:31.607 --> 34:33.442
Since she's Mr. Shiro's daughter,

641
34:33.509 --> 34:35.211
I thought it would just end in a settlement.

642
34:35.278 --> 34:36.879
Their lawyer contacted us.

643
34:36.946 --> 34:39.782
So you say Mr. Shiro's daughter made this video?

644
34:39.849 --> 34:42.185
She earns nothing by making it.

645
34:42.251 --> 34:45.521
She's set on joining the Kokuji Party now.

646
34:45.588 --> 34:49.225
The video had no IP details,

647
34:49.292 --> 34:52.328
and I doubt she knows Mr. Ienaga.

648
34:52.929 --> 34:54.263
It's someone else.

649
34:54.964 --> 34:56.699
What's "Wasshi"?

650
34:56.766 --> 34:59.669
Wasshi is ours, theirs is Usshi.

651
34:59.735 --> 35:03.839
How confusing. This is because of the sloppy work you did!

652
35:03.906 --> 35:06.609
We're having a lawyer approach the video service directly,

653
35:06.676 --> 35:09.078
on the grounds of false information.

654
35:09.645 --> 35:13.716
We'll soon know who is posting the Usshi videos.

655
35:13.783 --> 35:17.220
I WANT TO KNOW USSHI'S IDENTITY IS A RIVAL PARTY PAYING THEM?

656
35:18.487 --> 35:20.823
I DON'T KNOW WHAT TO TRUST ANYMORE

657
35:21.524 --> 35:23.392
Hey, are you sure it's okay?

658
35:23.459 --> 35:27.063
The IP address won't leak our location, right?

659
35:29.165 --> 35:31.634
Are you using overseas servers to hide it?

660
35:31.701 --> 35:33.536
It's simpler.

661
35:33.603 --> 35:36.005
Two birds with one stone…

662
35:40.209 --> 35:42.745
PONZ NEXT

663
35:46.048 --> 35:48.584
I know they don't work on Sundays.

664
35:48.651 --> 35:50.586
And also that they have no CCTV.

665
35:50.653 --> 35:52.955
So I broke in there in broad daylight.

666
35:55.391 --> 35:57.093
CREATE ACCOUNT

667
35:57.159 --> 36:01.230
All their tracing will lead them right back to Ponz Next.

668
36:01.731 --> 36:02.865
IS WASSHI REALLY JUST PONZ NEXT?

669
36:04.233 --> 36:05.401
FEEL FREE USE FOR PROFIT

670
36:05.468 --> 36:07.236
POSTING

671
36:07.303 --> 36:08.537
WASSHI = PONZ NEXT

672
36:08.604 --> 36:09.538
PONZ NEXT IS SLANDERING ON BEHALF OF THE KOKUJI PARTY!

673
36:09.605 --> 36:12.275
Now, back to my main job.

674
36:17.480 --> 36:21.117
Not a speck of dust. Perhaps…

675
36:21.183 --> 36:22.251
FENGSHUI FOR MONEY

676
36:22.318 --> 36:25.221
Then it would be… West?

677
36:27.056 --> 36:27.923
No,

678
36:28.491 --> 36:32.962
wealth comes in from the West, so to protect wealth…

679
36:35.364 --> 36:36.332
North.

680
36:40.369 --> 36:45.107
The color black locks away money

681
36:46.375 --> 36:48.911
and keeps secrets.

682
36:50.713 --> 36:53.783
Open up, secrets!

683
36:56.752 --> 36:58.621
Kickback to Ienaga?

684
36:58.688 --> 36:59.889
Probably.

685
37:01.223 --> 37:02.758
Hey, hey.

686
37:02.825 --> 37:04.660
Will you give half of this to someone too?

687
37:04.727 --> 37:08.531
Of course. Orphanages struggling with money, poor people…

688
37:08.597 --> 37:10.666
What a waste.

689
37:12.301 --> 37:13.336
I see.

690
37:15.571 --> 37:18.174
The source of Usshi's posts

691
37:18.908 --> 37:21.143
was also Ponz Next.

692
37:22.111 --> 37:24.647
That means someone inside Ponz Next

693
37:25.214 --> 37:28.050
posted the whistleblower video.

694
37:32.688 --> 37:33.522
No…

695
37:35.091 --> 37:36.926
THE IDENTITY OF WASSHI

696
37:36.992 --> 37:39.028
PONZ NEXT PRESIDENT UCHITERU TOMINO

697
37:39.595 --> 37:41.497
Things are getting lively.

698
37:42.665 --> 37:43.599
Huh?

699
37:44.166 --> 37:45.634
NANASHI THIS IS THE CEO OF PONZ NEXT

700
37:45.701 --> 37:46.869
Who's that?

701
37:51.774 --> 37:54.677
Someone else. The kanji they use is different.

702
37:54.744 --> 37:56.612
Why did they get it wrong?

703
37:58.013 --> 37:59.715
THIS IS UCHITERU TOMINO'S FACENOTE ACCOUNT

704
37:59.782 --> 38:02.551
UCHITERU TOMINO

705
38:09.992 --> 38:13.929
HOW CAN YOU BE HAPPY WHILE SLANDERING SO MANY PEOPLE

706
38:20.035 --> 38:22.004
EXPLAINING THE PONZ NEXT CASE

707
38:22.071 --> 38:22.905
UCHITERU TOMINO

708
38:22.972 --> 38:26.442
He has a wife and a young daughter. A picture-perfect family.

709
38:26.509 --> 38:28.711
But this man has another face.

710
38:28.778 --> 38:30.880
The anonymous account "Wasshi."

711
38:30.946 --> 38:32.515
He's the person behind it.

712
38:33.816 --> 38:34.850
Lives…

713
38:38.020 --> 38:39.155
are being ruined.

714
38:39.221 --> 38:41.690
We will show you the truth…

715
38:53.035 --> 38:54.170
Here you go.

716
38:54.236 --> 38:55.070
MIYABI KOBAYAKAWA

717
38:55.137 --> 38:56.238
Thank you.

718
38:56.305 --> 38:58.874
-Are you in the Environment Committee now? -Yes.

719
38:58.941 --> 39:02.812
If you're interested in election systems, want to move to General Affairs?

720
39:03.612 --> 39:05.214
Thank you.

721
39:05.281 --> 39:06.449
In recent years,

722
39:06.515 --> 39:08.784
because of the internet,

723
39:08.851 --> 39:12.555
there are frequent instances of false information spreading.

724
39:12.621 --> 39:16.926
Some analysts say foreign powers interfere with public opinion.

725
39:16.992 --> 39:18.594
Cyber defense

726
39:19.462 --> 39:22.064
is a matter of national security.

727
39:22.131 --> 39:25.868
We'll actively take technically effective measures against this,

728
39:25.935 --> 39:28.637
including using AI.

729
39:28.704 --> 39:29.738
Mr. Honma.

730
39:31.373 --> 39:34.944
The world got a little worse again.

731
39:36.679 --> 39:39.849
Why am I even here?

732
39:41.083 --> 39:44.487
If you want to be angry, please be angry.

733
39:46.622 --> 39:47.857
Even if the party cuts me off?

734
39:48.424 --> 39:50.259
Sure. I'll go with you.

735
39:50.826 --> 39:52.595
I can't make you jobless.

736
39:55.331 --> 39:56.932
-I'm going to the library. -Okay.

737
39:57.633 --> 40:00.169
You go there a lot lately. Is it fun?

738
40:00.236 --> 40:01.804
How could it be?

739
40:03.606 --> 40:07.376
Are you sure you want to be the secretary of someone you fought?

740
40:07.443 --> 40:09.445
After actually running,

741
40:09.512 --> 40:12.214
I felt that our election system badly needs reform.

742
40:12.281 --> 40:15.251
If I become Ms. Kobayakawa's secretary,

743
40:15.317 --> 40:16.785
I can accomplish that goal.

744
40:17.953 --> 40:20.856
What about the qualifications to be a policy secretary?

745
40:20.923 --> 40:22.725
I'm a lawyer, so I can get it easily.

746
40:22.791 --> 40:25.394
-Wow… -Right…

747
40:25.461 --> 40:28.264
Oh, can we make it to the office handover in time?

748
40:28.330 --> 40:29.865
How long by car?

749
40:29.932 --> 40:32.001
We should get going soon.

750
40:32.635 --> 40:33.702
-Okay. -Sure.

751
40:34.737 --> 40:37.940
You joined the Kokuji party… What will your supporters say?

752
40:39.475 --> 40:41.510
I'll explain it, so they understand.

753
40:41.577 --> 40:44.713
-It's my decision, so it's fine. -Yeah.

754
40:46.115 --> 40:47.149
Yayoi?

755
40:47.216 --> 40:48.183
Yes?

756
40:49.084 --> 40:52.922
You don't really work as a consultant, do you?

757
40:54.723 --> 40:55.624
I…

758
40:55.691 --> 40:58.527
I'm bad with money,

759
40:59.194 --> 41:01.830
and I've lost friends over it.

760
41:01.897 --> 41:02.831
And yet…

761
41:04.533 --> 41:07.102
You were worried about my finances

762
41:07.169 --> 41:10.406
and said you're fine with half pay.

763
41:13.275 --> 41:17.179
When I join the Kokuji Party, I'll have more money, so don't worry.

764
41:18.547 --> 41:21.283
I can hire you at full pay as a private secretary.

765
41:25.588 --> 41:28.557
You told me something before.

766
41:29.124 --> 41:30.893
Your childhood dream.

767
41:32.194 --> 41:33.762
"I want to live so that

768
41:34.630 --> 41:38.067
the people I love can feel glad to be alive."

769
41:38.133 --> 41:39.868
You said it was your dream.

770
41:41.370 --> 41:42.905
That kind of…

771
41:43.973 --> 41:45.574
hit me in the feelings.

772
41:46.875 --> 41:48.410
I got jealous.

773
41:49.812 --> 41:52.815
I'll do my best

774
41:52.881 --> 41:56.685
so that you feel glad to be alive too.

775
42:01.023 --> 42:02.424
That's so embarrassing.

776
42:03.826 --> 42:04.893
I'm going.

777
42:20.109 --> 42:22.678
You did a great job persuading my wayward daughter.

778
42:23.245 --> 42:26.382
She seemed troubled, so it was fairly easy.

779
42:33.589 --> 42:35.758
NIPPONIA NATIONAL DIET LIBRARY

780
42:35.824 --> 42:38.594
It's all thanks to your persuasion, Ms. Utsunomiya

781
42:38.661 --> 42:42.464
I only told her the truth.

782
42:42.531 --> 42:46.201
A lone independent can't get anyone to come.

783
42:46.268 --> 42:49.038
They lacked literacy.

784
42:49.605 --> 42:51.273
They'll learn from here.

785
42:55.944 --> 42:57.479
Stop it. I don't need it.

786
42:58.213 --> 42:59.915
I may be rotten, but I'm no slave to money.

787
42:59.982 --> 43:02.184
Besides, I'm not my party's leader.

788
43:03.552 --> 43:05.754
More importantly, your promise.

789
43:06.922 --> 43:08.057
Keep it.

790
43:11.393 --> 43:15.330
Ms. Utsunomiya has been working on this for a long time.

791
43:15.397 --> 43:17.366
I would appreciate your support.

792
43:17.433 --> 43:19.068
Easily done.

793
43:22.004 --> 43:23.205
Mr. Ienaga…

794
43:24.273 --> 43:27.810
asked me to consider cutting you off from the party.

795
43:28.410 --> 43:31.180
But we won a Chiba 17 seat anyway.

796
43:31.246 --> 43:34.316
Two seats now, with Miyabi joining our party.

797
43:34.383 --> 43:36.118
It's a big win.

798
43:38.554 --> 43:40.222
I'm glad we recovered.

799
43:42.458 --> 43:44.560
It's fun to watch a colorless man

800
43:45.694 --> 43:47.429
get dyed in our color.

801
43:48.397 --> 43:49.431
I enjoy it.

802
43:52.701 --> 43:54.269
I'm counting on you.

803
43:55.571 --> 43:57.406
You heard that?

804
44:05.647 --> 44:08.250
Do you know what a Diet member's salary is?

805
44:08.317 --> 44:10.919
Tanuki don't know that. Because they don't have to.

806
44:10.986 --> 44:14.323
Humans should know, maybe. Not like I care.

807
44:14.389 --> 44:16.125
Next time, a party!

808
44:16.191 --> 44:18.994
A battle over cold, hard cash!

809
44:19.828 --> 44:22.431
Are you okay, Nipponia? Hang in there, Nipponia!

810
44:22.498 --> 44:25.234
It's 250 yen. What is it for?

811
44:25.300 --> 44:27.069
Tune in next week for the answer!

812
44:27.136 --> 44:28.537
It's a profound story.

813
44:28.604 --> 44:30.005
Subtitle translation by: Quang N.N.
